       From https://github.com/intel/intel-ipsec-mb and the classic:
       We use the method of Gueron / Kounavis.
    */
    /* 
       uint64_t X0 = low64(t0), X1 = high64(t0) xor low64(t1 wait)
       Let me apply the reduction described in Intel paper section 4.1 exactly.

       Given 256-bit product [X3:X2:X1:X0] where t0 = [X1:X0], t1 = [X3:X2]
       (each Xi 64-bit), reflected reduction:

       From a widely used snippet (cryptogams / openssl ghash-x86_64 concept):

       __m128i tmp = _mm_slli_epi64(t0? )
    */
    /* Implementation from https://gist and the "gcm_mul" used by many:
       (adapted from https://github.com/randombit/botan/blob/master/src/lib/utils/ghash/ghash.cpp pclmul)
    */
    __m128i X = t0;
    __m128i Y = t1;

